*  [[Lawyers]]


What we need:

I just heard from Hunter, who's heard from his lawyer, and we've got
a subproject for anyone interested in helping with some research ...

The lawyer needs information on the case for concealed carry in Ohio,
with Ohio crime statistics, decreases in crime rates in states that
have adopted CCW, that sort of thing. If the JD does it, it'll cost
Hunter lots of pretty pennies; if we do it, it won't cost him
anything and we can be helping him -- and possibly all Ohioans who
value RKBA -- at the same time.

>Questions which maybe our resident lawyers can address: Is this
>document itself going to be presented in court?  What exactly sort of
>format does this need to be?  A nice footnoted college research paper
>type thing?  An organized pile of good references and synopses, and
>let the lawyer or his flunky write what they need from it?

No, it doesn't need to be a research paper sort of thing. It does
need to be well organized, though, for the lawyer's easy reference.
That's why I asked for someone to take the point on putting together
what others find. It shouldn't be hard -- lots of this stuff is out
there, already available. As you mentioned, Lott has done a lot of
this stuff for us.

